{"p07-l01":[{"id":"p07-l01-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Worst-case total of 0.5, 1.5, 0.25 and 0.1 % FS?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Add the magnitudes.</p>\n","answer":2.35,"tol":0.001,"unit":"% FS"},{"id":"p07-l01-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>RSS total of the same four errors?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Root of the sum of squares.</p>\n","answer":1.6035,"tol":0.002,"unit":"% FS"},{"id":"p07-l01-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Averaging many readings removes…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The mean converges to truth plus bias.</p>\n","options":["bias","random scatter, but not bias","hysteresis","gain error"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l01-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Sensitivity in mV/kPa of a 0–100 kPa sensor with a 0.5–4.5 V output?</p>\n","explain":"<p>4 V over 100 kPa.</p>\n","answer":40,"tol":0.001,"unit":"mV/kPa"},{"id":"p07-l01-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Different outputs for the same input approached from above and below is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It depends on the history.</p>\n","options":["non-linearity","hysteresis","noise","offset"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l01-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Noise in kPa after averaging 16 readings of 0.05 kPa rms noise?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Divide by √16.</p>\n","answer":0.0125,"tol":0.001,"unit":"kPa"}],"p07-l02":[{"id":"p07-l02-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Gain in counts/kg from 1012 counts at 0 kg and 53 412 counts at 5 kg?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Rise over run.</p>\n","answer":10480,"tol":0.001,"unit":"counts/kg"},{"id":"p07-l02-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Mass in kg for a reading of 22 000 counts?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Subtract the offset, divide by the gain.</p>\n","answer":2.00267,"tol":0.001,"unit":"kg"},{"id":"p07-l02-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Residuals that form a smooth bow indicate…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Noise doesn’t have a shape.</p>\n","options":["random noise","non-linearity the model doesn’t capture","a perfect fit","an offset error"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l02-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Least squares improves on a two-point calibration because…</p>\n","explain":"<p>More data and a diagnostic.</p>\n","options":["it needs no references","noise averages over many points, and residuals can be inspected","it is always exact","it removes hysteresis"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l02-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Uncertainty in counts/kg of a two-point slope over 5 kg with 20 counts rms noise per reading?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Two independent readings.</p>\n","answer":5.657,"tol":0.002,"unit":"counts/kg"},{"id":"p07-l02-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>0.1 % of a 5 kg full scale in grams?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The spec used in the code.</p>\n","answer":5,"tol":0.001,"unit":"g"}],"p07-l03":[{"id":"p07-l03-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Loaded output ratio at x = 2/3 with k = 10?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The loading formula.</p>\n","answer":0.65217,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l03-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Approximate worst loading error in % for k = 10?</p>\n","explain":"<p>About 15/k %.</p>\n","answer":1.5,"tol":0.05,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p07-l03-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>The loading error peaks at about…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> is largest.</p>\n","options":["x = 0","x = 1/2","x = 2/3","x = 1"],"answer":2},{"id":"p07-l03-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Angle resolution in degrees of a 300° pot on a 12-bit ADC?</p>\n","explain":"<p>In principle, before noise and linearity.</p>\n","answer":0.073242,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l03-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The simplest way to remove loading error is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Very high input resistance.</p>\n","options":["a bigger pot","a voltage-follower buffer","a lower supply","a longer cable"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l03-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Maximum pot value in kΩ for &lt; 0.5 % error into 100 kΩ (using 15/k)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>k ≥ 30.</p>\n","answer":3.333,"tol":0.002,"unit":"kΩ"}],"p07-l04":[{"id":"p07-l04-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>ΔR/R in % for GF = 2 and 1000 µε?</p>\n","explain":"<p>GF × strain.</p>\n","answer":0.2,"tol":0.001,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p07-l04-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Full-scale output in mV of a 2 mV/V load cell at 3.3 V excitation?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Sensitivity × excitation.</p>\n","answer":6.6,"tol":0.001,"unit":"mV"},{"id":"p07-l04-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Maximum INA gain with 1.65 V headroom and 6.6 mV full scale?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Headroom over signal.</p>\n","answer":250,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l04-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Grams per count with G = 200 and a 16-bit ADC (5 kg, 2 mV/V, ratiometric)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>5243 counts per kg.</p>\n","answer":0.19073,"tol":0.002,"unit":"g"},{"id":"p07-l04-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A full bridge with two stretched and two compressed gauges…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Compared with a single gauge.</p>\n","options":["quadruples the signal and cancels temperature drift","needs no excitation","removes the need for an amplifier","halves the signal"],"answer":0},{"id":"p07-l04-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Ratiometric measurement means…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The ratio cancels supply variation.</p>\n","options":["the ADC reference also excites the sensor","two ADCs are used","the gain is unity","the signal is AC"],"answer":0}],"p07-l05":[{"id":"p07-l05-q1","type":"mc","q":"<p>The Steinhart-Hart equation models…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Three coefficients.</p>\n","options":["R as a polynomial in T","1/T as A + B ln R + C (ln R)^3","T as linear in R","the β value only"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l05-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Minimum number of table points to determine A, B and C?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Three unknowns.</p>\n","answer":3,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l05-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Self-heating power in µW of a 10 kΩ thermistor with 1.65 V across it?</p>\n","explain":"<p>V²/R.</p>\n","answer":272.25,"tol":0.002,"unit":"µW"},{"id":"p07-l05-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Thermistor resistance in kΩ when a 12-bit divider (10 kΩ fixed, thermistor low) reads 2048?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Mid-scale means equal resistances.</p>\n","answer":10,"tol":0.001,"unit":"kΩ"},{"id":"p07-l05-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The β equation is exact…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It’s a two-point model.</p>\n","options":["everywhere","only at its two defining temperatures","only at 0 °C","never"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l05-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Approximate self-heating in K at 1 mK/µW and 272 µW?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Comparable to the accuracy target.</p>\n","answer":0.272,"tol":0.01,"unit":"K"}],"p07-l06":[{"id":"p07-l06-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>PT100 resistance in Ω at 100 °C?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Callendar-Van Dusen.</p>\n","answer":138.5055,"tol":0.001,"unit":"Ω"},{"id":"p07-l06-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Compensated voltage in mV for 15.396 mV with terminals at 25 °C (E(25) = 1.000 mV)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Add E of the cold junction.</p>\n","answer":16.396,"tol":0.001,"unit":"mV"},{"id":"p07-l06-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>A thermocouple’s voltage depends on…</p>\n","explain":"<p>V = E(T_hot) − E(T_cold).</p>\n","options":["the hot junction only","the temperature difference between hot and cold junctions","the wire length","the current through it"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l06-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Temperature error in K from 1 Ω of lead resistance on a PT100 (0.39 Ω/K)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Use 4 wires.</p>\n","answer":2.564,"tol":0.01,"unit":"K"},{"id":"p07-l06-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Approximate type K sensitivity in µV/K?</p>\n","explain":"<p>About 41 µV/K near room temperature.</p>\n","answer":41,"tol":0.05,"unit":"µV/K"},{"id":"p07-l06-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>CJC needs…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A thermistor or IC sensor at the terminals.</p>\n","options":["a second thermocouple","a separate measurement of the terminal temperature","an ice bath always","a higher ADC resolution only"],"answer":1}],"p07-l07":[{"id":"p07-l07-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Frequency-method resolution in rev/s for 2000 counts/rev and a 1 ms window?</p>\n","explain":"<p>One count per window.</p>\n","answer":0.5,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rev/s"},{"id":"p07-l07-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Timer ticks per count at 2 rev/s with a 10 MHz timer?</p>\n","explain":"<p>f_t over the count rate.</p>\n","answer":2500,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l07-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Crossover speed in rev/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Where both resolutions are equal.</p>\n","answer":50,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rev/s"},{"id":"p07-l07-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>At very low speed, prefer…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Many timer ticks per edge.</p>\n","options":["the frequency method","the period method","[object Object]","a bigger window only"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l07-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Period-method resolution in % at 80 rev/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>ωN/f_t.</p>\n","answer":1.6,"tol":0.001,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p07-l07-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The M/T method…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It gets the best of both.</p>\n","options":["counts edges and times the window from the first to the last edge","uses two encoders","averages the two estimates","only works at standstill"],"answer":0}],"p07-l08":[{"id":"p07-l08-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Hall transitions per second for 4 pole pairs at 3000 rpm?</p>\n","explain":"<p>6 per electrical revolution.</p>\n","answer":1200,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l08-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Hall voltage in mV for I = 1 mA, B = 0.1 T, n = 1e21 m⁻³, t = 10 µm?</p>\n","explain":"<p>V_H = IB/(nqt).</p>\n","answer":62.42,"tol":0.005,"unit":"mV"},{"id":"p07-l08-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Which Hall codes indicate a fault?</p>\n","explain":"<p>They never occur in normal rotation.</p>\n","options":["101 and 010","000 and 111","100 and 011","none"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l08-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Minimum six-step torque as a percentage of peak?</p>\n","explain":"<p>cos 30°.</p>\n","answer":86.6,"tol":0.001,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p07-l08-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>In six-step drive, during each sector…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Two phases conduct.</p>\n","options":["all three phases conduct","one phase is high, one low and one floating","only one phase conducts","the phases are sinusoidal"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l08-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Transitions per mechanical revolution for 7 pole pairs?</p>\n","explain":"<p>6p.</p>\n","answer":42,"tol":0.001,"unit":""}],"p07-l09":[{"id":"p07-l09-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Pitch in degrees for a_x = 0.342 g and a_z = 0.940 g (a_y = 0)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>atan2.</p>\n","answer":19.997,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l09-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>False pitch in degrees from 0.1 g of forward acceleration?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Acceleration is indistinguishable from tilt.</p>\n","answer":5.7106,"tol":0.001,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l09-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>At rest on a level table, an accelerometer’s z axis reads…</p>\n","explain":"<p>It measures specific force.</p>\n","options":["0 g","+1 g (up)","−1 g","9.81 g"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l09-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Deflection in nm of a 5 kHz proof mass under 1 g?</p>\n","explain":"<p>a/ω².</p>\n","answer":9.94,"tol":0.01,"unit":"nm"},{"id":"p07-l09-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>atan2 is used instead of atan because…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Full ±180° range.</p>\n","options":["it is faster","it handles all quadrants and a zero denominator","it removes noise","it gives yaw"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l09-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Scatter in degrees after averaging 100 readings with 1.1° per reading?</p>\n","explain":"<p>√N.</p>\n","answer":0.11,"tol":0.001,"unit":"°"}],"p07-l10":[{"id":"p07-l10-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Heading error in degrees after 60 s from a 0.5 °/s bias?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Linear growth.</p>\n","answer":30,"tol":0.001,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l10-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Bias uncertainty in °/s after 10 s at rest with N = 0.01 °/s/√Hz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>N/√T.</p>\n","answer":0.0031623,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°/s"},{"id":"p07-l10-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Coriolis acceleration in m/s² for 100 °/s and 0.1 m/s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>2Ωv.</p>\n","answer":0.34907,"tol":0.002,"unit":"m/s²"},{"id":"p07-l10-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>The angle error from white gyro noise grows like…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A random walk.</p>\n","options":["t","√t","t²","it doesn’t grow"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l10-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Seconds at rest for a bias uncertainty of 0.001 °/s with N = 0.01 °/s/√Hz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>T = (N/σ)².</p>\n","answer":100,"tol":0.001,"unit":"s"},{"id":"p07-l10-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>After subtracting an estimated bias, heading drift is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Residual bias and random walk remain.</p>\n","options":["eliminated forever","smaller but still unbounded","larger","bounded by 1°"],"answer":1}],"p07-l11":[{"id":"p07-l11-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Raw heading in degrees for m_x = 37 µT, m_y = −23 µT?</p>\n","explain":"<p>atan2(−m_y, m_x).</p>\n","answer":31.866,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l11-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Corrected heading in degrees after removing an offset of (15, −8) µT?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Subtract the offset first.</p>\n","answer":34.287,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l11-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Hard iron…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A constant offset vector.</p>\n","options":["stretches the sphere of readings","shifts its centre","rotates the Earth’s field","adds noise"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l11-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Soft iron turns the sphere of readings into…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A linear map.</p>\n","options":["a shifted sphere","an ellipsoid","a plane","a line"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l11-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Unknowns in the linear ellipsoid fit?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Six quadratic and three linear terms.</p>\n","answer":9,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l11-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Magnitude in µT of a field of (20, 0, −40) µT?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Typical for mid-latitudes.</p>\n","answer":44.721,"tol":0.002,"unit":"µT"}],"p07-l12":[{"id":"p07-l12-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Speed of sound in m/s at 20 °C?</p>\n","explain":"<p>331.3 + 0.606 T.</p>\n","answer":343.42,"tol":0.001,"unit":"m/s"},{"id":"p07-l12-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Distance in m for an 11.66 ms round trip at 20 °C?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Half the round trip.</p>\n","answer":2.0021,"tol":0.001,"unit":"m"},{"id":"p07-l12-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Range per 40 kHz cycle in mm (c = 343 m/s)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Half a wavelength.</p>\n","answer":4.2875,"tol":0.002,"unit":"mm"},{"id":"p07-l12-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Cross-correlation beats a fixed threshold because…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A matched filter.</p>\n","options":["it is faster","it uses the whole echo and doesn’t depend on amplitude","it needs no transmitted signal","it removes the speed of sound"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l12-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Range error in % from assuming 343 m/s when the air is at 0 °C?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Measure the temperature.</p>\n","answer":3.53,"tol":0.01,"unit":"%"},{"id":"p07-l12-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Fitting a parabola to the correlation peak gives…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Interpolation between samples.</p>\n","options":["sub-sample time resolution","the speed of sound","the echo amplitude only","a wider beam"],"answer":0}],"p07-l13":[{"id":"p07-l13-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Ambiguity distance in m at 20 MHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>c/(2f).</p>\n","answer":7.4948,"tol":0.001,"unit":"m"},{"id":"p07-l13-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Distance in m for a 1.2 rad phase at 20 MHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>cΔφ/(4πf).</p>\n","answer":1.4313,"tol":0.001,"unit":"m"},{"id":"p07-l13-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Unambiguous range in m of 20 and 25 MHz combined?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Their difference, 5 MHz.</p>\n","answer":29.979,"tol":0.001,"unit":"m"},{"id":"p07-l13-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Round-trip time in ps for 1 mm of range?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Light is fast.</p>\n","answer":6.6713,"tol":0.002,"unit":"ps"},{"id":"p07-l13-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A LiDAR range of exactly 0 usually means…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Filter invalid returns.</p>\n","options":["an object touching the sensor","no return; discard it","maximum precision","a mixed pixel"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l13-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>The y coordinate in m of a return at 30° and 2.31 m?</p>\n","explain":"<p>r sin θ.</p>\n","answer":1.155,"tol":0.001,"unit":"m"}],"p07-l14":[{"id":"p07-l14-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Shunt resistance in mΩ for 50 mV at 20 A?</p>\n","explain":"<p>R = V/I.</p>\n","answer":2.5,"tol":0.001,"unit":"mΩ"},{"id":"p07-l14-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Power in W at 20 A through 2.5 mΩ?</p>\n","explain":"<p>I²R.</p>\n","answer":1,"tol":0.001,"unit":"W"},{"id":"p07-l14-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Amplifier gain to map ±50 mV onto 0–3.3 V around mid-rail?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Half the span over the