re","ADC resolution"],"answer":0}],"p07-l16":[{"id":"p07-l16-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Attenuation in dB needed to keep a full-scale alias below 1 LSB at 12 bits?</p>\n","explain":"<p>20 log₁₀ 2^(N−1).</p>\n","answer":66.227,"tol":0.001,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p07-l16-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Frequency in Hz where 900 Hz appears when sampled at 1 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>It folds about f_s/2.</p>\n","answer":100,"tol":0.001,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p07-l16-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Attenuation in dB of a 4th-order Butterworth (f_c = 100 Hz) at 900 Hz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>10 log₁₀(1 + (f/f_c)^(2n)).</p>\n","answer":76.335,"tol":0.002,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p07-l16-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>An alias already in the sampled data can be removed by…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Filter before sampling.</p>\n","options":["a digital low-pass filter","[object Object]","a higher ADC resolution","averaging"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l16-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Minimum Butterworth order for 66.2 dB at 9× the corner?</p>\n","explain":"<p>About 19.1 dB per order.</p>\n","answer":4,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l16-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>The usual modern alternative to a steep analogue filter is…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Moves the aliases far away.</p>\n","options":["a slower ADC","oversampling, then digital filtering and decimation","removing the filter","a higher reference voltage"],"answer":1}],"p07-l17":[{"id":"p07-l17-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Ideal SNR in dB of a 12-bit ADC?</p>\n","explain":"<p>6.02N + 1.76.</p>\n","answer":74,"tol":0.001,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p07-l17-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Quantisation noise in mV rms for a 12-bit, 3.3 V ADC?</p>\n","explain":"<p>q/√12.</p>\n","answer":0.23262,"tol":0.002,"unit":"mV"},{"id":"p07-l17-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>ENOB of an ADC with 86 dB SINAD?</p>\n","explain":"<p>(SINAD − 1.76)/6.02.</p>\n","answer":13.993,"tol":0.002,"unit":"bits"},{"id":"p07-l17-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Coherent sampling means…</p>\n","explain":"<p>No leakage.</p>\n","options":["sampling twice per cycle","an integer (ideally prime) number of cycles in the record","using a Hann window","sampling at the signal frequency"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l17-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>SNR gain in dB from averaging 16 samples of uncorrelated noise?</p>\n","explain":"<p>10 log₁₀ M.</p>\n","answer":12.041,"tol":0.002,"unit":"dB"},{"id":"p07-l17-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Variance of a uniform error over one LSB, in units of q²?</p>\n","explain":"<p>q²/12.</p>\n","answer":0.083333,"tol":0.001,"unit":""}],"p07-l18":[{"id":"p07-l18-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>α for τ = 0.5 s at 200 Hz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>τ/(τ + Δt).</p>\n","answer":0.9901,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l18-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Steady error in degrees from a 1.5 °/s gyro bias with τ = 0.5 s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>bτ.</p>\n","answer":0.75,"tol":0.001,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l18-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>In a complementary filter, the gyro contributes…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Its errors are low-frequency drift.</p>\n","options":["the low frequencies","the high frequencies","only the bias","nothing"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l18-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>The two filters must sum to one so that…</p>\n","explain":"<p>That’s what complementary means.</p>\n","options":["noise doubles","the true signal passes undistorted at every frequency","the gyro bias vanishes","α is zero"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l18-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Crossover frequency in Hz for τ = 0.5 s?</p>\n","explain":"<p>1/(2πτ).</p>\n","answer":0.31831,"tol":0.002,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p07-l18-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Gyro-only drift in degrees after 20 s with a 1.5 °/s bias?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Linear growth.</p>\n","answer":30,"tol":0.001,"unit":"°"}]}